WEBVTT

00:00.580 --> 00:02.230
We're asked to
complete the square

00:02.230 --> 00:08.950
to solve 4x squared plus
40x minus 300 is equal to 0.

00:08.950 --> 00:10.240
So let me just rewrite it.

00:10.240 --> 00:17.830
So 4x squared plus 40x
minus 300 is equal to 0.

00:17.830 --> 00:19.890
So just as a first
step here, I don't

00:19.890 --> 00:22.204
like having this 4 out
front as a coefficient

00:22.204 --> 00:23.120
on the x squared term.

00:23.120 --> 00:25.100
I'd prefer if that was a 1.

00:25.100 --> 00:28.180
So let's just divide both
sides of this equation by 4.

00:28.180 --> 00:30.480
So let's just divide
everything by 4.

00:30.480 --> 00:32.900
So this divided
by 4, this divided

00:32.900 --> 00:35.710
by 4, that divided by 4,
and the 0 divided by 4.

00:35.710 --> 00:37.720
Just dividing both sides by 4.

00:37.720 --> 00:42.050
So this will simplify
to x squared plus 10x.

00:42.050 --> 00:44.892
And I can obviously
do that, because

00:44.892 --> 00:46.850
as long as whatever I do
to the left hand side,

00:46.850 --> 00:48.440
I also do the right
hand side, that

00:48.440 --> 00:51.570
will make the equality
continue to be valid.

00:51.570 --> 00:53.030
So that's why I can do that.

00:53.030 --> 00:55.280
So 40 divided by 4 is 10x.

00:55.280 --> 00:58.440
And then 300 divided
by 4 is what?

00:58.440 --> 01:00.090
That is 75.

01:00.090 --> 01:03.700
Let me verify that.

01:03.700 --> 01:05.239
4 goes into 30 seven times.

01:05.239 --> 01:07.100
7 times 4 is 28.

01:07.100 --> 01:08.740
You subtract, you
get a remainder of 2.

01:08.740 --> 01:09.660
Bring down the 0.

01:09.660 --> 01:11.720
4 goes into 20 five times.

01:11.720 --> 01:13.430
5 times 4 is 20.

01:13.430 --> 01:14.580
Subtract zero.

01:14.580 --> 01:16.340
So it goes 75 times.

01:16.340 --> 01:21.520
This is minus 75 is equal to 0.

01:21.520 --> 01:24.340
And right when you look at
this, just the way it's written,

01:24.340 --> 01:26.860
you might try to factor
this in some way.

01:26.860 --> 01:29.370
But it's pretty clear this
is not a complete square,

01:29.370 --> 01:31.347
or this is not a perfect
square trinomial.

01:31.347 --> 01:33.180
Because if you look at
this term right here,

01:33.180 --> 01:36.450
this 10, half of this 10 is 5.

01:36.450 --> 01:40.050
And 5 squared is not 75.

01:40.050 --> 01:41.490
So this is not a perfect square.

01:41.490 --> 01:43.957
So what we want to
do is somehow turn

01:43.957 --> 01:45.540
whatever we have on
the left hand side

01:45.540 --> 01:47.310
into a perfect square.

01:47.310 --> 01:50.060
And I'm going to start out by
kind of getting this 75 out

01:50.060 --> 01:50.560
of the way.

01:50.560 --> 01:52.059
You'll sometimes
see it where people

01:52.059 --> 01:53.786
leave the 75 on
the left hand side.

01:53.786 --> 01:55.410
I'm going to put on
the right hand side

01:55.410 --> 01:57.630
just so it kind of clears
things up a little bit.

01:57.630 --> 02:00.810
So let's add 75 to both
sides to get rid of the 75

02:00.810 --> 02:03.800
from the left hand
side of the equation.

02:03.800 --> 02:08.610
And so we get x squared plus
10x, and then negative 75

02:08.610 --> 02:09.229
plus 75.

02:09.229 --> 02:10.345
Those guys cancel out.

02:10.345 --> 02:11.970
And I'm going to
leave some space here,

02:11.970 --> 02:13.678
because we're going
to add something here

02:13.678 --> 02:16.580
to complete the square
that is equal to 75.

02:16.580 --> 02:19.970
So all I did is add 75 to
both sides of this equation.

02:19.970 --> 02:21.880
Now, in this step,
this is really

02:21.880 --> 02:23.860
the meat of
completing the square.

02:23.860 --> 02:27.000
I want to add something to
both sides of this equation.

02:27.000 --> 02:29.550
I can't add to only one
side of the equation.

02:29.550 --> 02:32.240
So I want to add something to
both sides of this equation

02:32.240 --> 02:35.370
so that this left hand side
becomes a perfect square.

02:35.370 --> 02:38.410
And the way we can do that,
and saw this in the last video

02:38.410 --> 02:41.040
where we constructed a
perfect square trinomial,

02:41.040 --> 02:43.660
is that this last
term-- or I should

02:43.660 --> 02:46.110
say, what we see on
the left hand side, not

02:46.110 --> 02:48.720
the last term, this expression
on the left hand side,

02:48.720 --> 02:53.210
it will be a perfect square if
we have a constant term that

02:53.210 --> 02:58.050
is the square of half of the
coefficient on the first degree

02:58.050 --> 02:58.780
term.

02:58.780 --> 03:00.900
So the coefficient here is 10.

03:00.900 --> 03:02.830
Half of 10 is 5.

03:02.830 --> 03:05.200
5 squared is 25.

03:05.200 --> 03:07.574
So I'm going to add 25
to the left hand side.

03:07.574 --> 03:09.990
And of course, in order to
maintain the equality, anything

03:09.990 --> 03:12.430
I do the left hand
side, I also have

03:12.430 --> 03:15.435
to do to the right hand side.

03:15.435 --> 03:17.310
And now we see that this
is a perfect square.

03:17.310 --> 03:19.940
We say, hey, what two numbers
if I add them I get 10

03:19.940 --> 03:21.920
and when I multiply
them I get 25?

03:21.920 --> 03:23.570
Well, that's 5 and 5.

03:23.570 --> 03:26.380
So when we factor this, what
we see on the left hand side

03:26.380 --> 03:30.150
simplifies to, this
is x plus 5 squared.

03:30.150 --> 03:33.250
x plus 5 times x plus 5.

03:33.250 --> 03:36.110
And you can look at
the videos on factoring

03:36.110 --> 03:38.312
if you find that confusing.

03:38.312 --> 03:39.770
Or you could look
at the last video

03:39.770 --> 03:42.477
on constructing perfect
square trinomials.

03:42.477 --> 03:44.060
I encourage you to
square this and see

03:44.060 --> 03:46.060
that you get exactly this.

03:46.060 --> 03:51.060
And this will be equal to 75
plus 25, which is equal to 100.

03:51.060 --> 03:53.290
And so now we're saying
that something squared

03:53.290 --> 03:55.110
is equal to 100.

03:55.110 --> 03:57.100
So really, this is
something right over here--

03:57.100 --> 03:59.100
if I say something squared
is equal to 100, that

03:59.100 --> 04:02.500
means that that something is
one of the square roots of 100.

04:02.500 --> 04:04.630
And we know that 100
has two square roots.

04:04.630 --> 04:07.840
It has positive 10 and
it has negative 10.

04:07.840 --> 04:10.050
So we could say that x
plus 5, the something

04:10.050 --> 04:12.010
that we were
squaring, that must be

04:12.010 --> 04:14.220
one of the square roots of 100.

04:14.220 --> 04:16.540
So that must be equal to the
plus or minus square root

04:16.540 --> 04:20.293
of 100, or plus or minus 10.

04:20.293 --> 04:21.459
Or we could separate it out.

04:21.459 --> 04:25.250
We could say that x
plus 5 is equal to 10,

04:25.250 --> 04:30.340
or x plus 5 is equal
to negative 10.

04:30.340 --> 04:32.390
On this side right
here, I can just

04:32.390 --> 04:35.010
subtract 5 from both
sides of this equation

04:35.010 --> 04:36.990
and I would get-- I'll
just write it out.

04:36.990 --> 04:41.790
Subtracting 5 from both
sides, I get x is equal to 5.

04:41.790 --> 04:43.240
And over here, I
could subtract 5

04:43.240 --> 04:47.810
from both sides again-- I
subtracted 5 in both cases--

04:47.810 --> 04:52.330
subtract 5 again and I can
get x is equal to negative 15.

04:52.330 --> 04:56.530
So those are my two
solutions that I

04:56.530 --> 04:58.320
got to solve this equation.

04:58.320 --> 05:02.230
We can verify that they actually
work, and I'll do that in blue.

05:02.230 --> 05:05.800
So let's try with 5.

05:05.800 --> 05:06.990
I'll just do one of them.

05:06.990 --> 05:08.850
I'll leave the
other one for you.

05:08.850 --> 05:11.450
I'll leave the other one for
you to verify that it works.

05:11.450 --> 05:15.180
So 4 times x squared.

05:15.180 --> 05:23.330
So 4 times 25 plus
40 times 5 minus 300

05:23.330 --> 05:24.860
needs to be equal to 0.

05:24.860 --> 05:26.762
4 times 25 is 100.

05:26.762 --> 05:28.920
40 times 5 is 200.

05:28.920 --> 05:30.570
We're going to
subtract that 300.

05:30.570 --> 05:34.770
100 plus 200 minus 300,
that definitely equals 0.

05:34.770 --> 05:36.310
So x equals 5 worked.

05:36.310 --> 05:39.330
And I think you'll find that
x equals negative 15 will also

05:39.330 --> 05:44.120
work when you substitute it
into this right over here.
